## Tech stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Runtime | .NET 10 (LTS, supported to Nov 2028) |
| SDK pin | 10.0.113 (pinned in `global.json`; re-verify before each release) |
| Language | C# 14, nullable reference types enabled |
| Build | `dotnet` CLI + NuGet |
| Test | xUnit v3 + `dotnet test` |
| Mocking | NSubstitute (not Moq) |
| Analysis | Roslyn analyzers + `.editorconfig`, warnings as errors |
| Platform | Fedora, local tools only, no containers |

## Platform rules

- **No containers.** No Containerfile, no Dockerfile, no Testcontainers. Build,
  test, and run on the local machine with the `dotnet` CLI.
- **No Windows, no Visual Studio.** Editor is VS Code + C# Dev Kit, or Rider.
  Every action is a `dotnet` CLI command; there is no "press F5" or `.sln`
  double-click step.
- **Case-sensitive filesystem, `/` paths, LF line endings.** Namespaces and file
  names must match case.

## How to run

```bash
dotnet run --project src/{{PROJECT_NAME}}        # run the app
```

## How to test

```bash
dotnet test                                      # restore, build, run all tests
dotnet test --filter "FullyQualifiedName~{{FILTER}}"   # a subset
```

## How to build and check

```bash
dotnet build                                     # warnings are errors; analyzers run
dotnet format --verify-no-changes                # style gate (non-zero if unformatted)
dotnet list package --outdated                   # flag pins that have moved
./scripts/check-prereqs.sh                        # verify the toolchain is present
```

## Key file locations

```
global.json                       ← pins the .NET SDK (10.0.113)
Directory.Build.props             ← shared build settings (LangVersion, Nullable, analyzers)
Directory.Packages.props          ← central NuGet version pins (if using CPM)
.editorconfig                     ← style + analyzer severities, LF line endings
src/{{PROJECT_NAME}}/             ← application code
tests/{{PROJECT_NAME}}.Tests/     ← xUnit v3 + NSubstitute tests
scripts/check-prereqs.sh          ← toolchain gate (exits non-zero if missing)
logs/                             ← rotating log files (gitignored)
```

## Logging

The app logs through `ILogger<T>` to the console and to a rotating file under
`logs/`. Read the current file with `Read logs/app-<date>.log` or
`grep -n 'ERR\|WRN\|Exception' logs/app-<date>.log` after a failure.

## Conventions

- Nullable reference types are on; a possible-null dereference fails the build.
- Pin every NuGet package to a stable version; survey with
  `dotnet package search <id>` before bumping. No prereleases, no floating ranges.
- Use NSubstitute for mocking. Do not add Moq.
